Adverse events
--------------

Time to onset per report and drug, derived from the FAERS quarterly files (Time machine)
  Publisher: U.S. Food and Drug Administration (derived by Janus)
  License: CC0 1.0
  Derived from the raw archives of the current faers run (THER.start_dt,
  DEMO.event_dt); only complete dates; exclusions counted by reason. Spontaneous
  reports: what reporters wrote down, not measured latency.
  A side table keeps DRUG.route and DRUG.dose_form as published and the
  exclusion reason of every report-drug pair (FAERS onset table for the PIPC
  rows).

FDA Adverse Event Monitoring System (AEMS, formerly FAERS) quarterly data files
  Publisher: U.S. Food and Drug Administration
  License: CC0 1.0
  Spontaneous reports; not deduplicated across cases; counts are reports, not
  people.
  Event terms are MedDRA Preferred Terms as published in FAERS. MedDRA® the
  Medical Dictionary for Regulatory Activities terminology is the international
  medical terminology developed under the auspices of ICH. MedDRA® trademark is
  registered by IFPMA on behalf of ICH. Not an FDA endorsement.

Official channels for reporting a suspected side effect (TİTCK/TÜFAM, FDA MedWatch, EMA, BfArM/PEI, ANSM, AEMPS)
  License: Janus curation (Apache-2.0); field labels quoted as published in
  public official forms
  Addresses, form ids and short field labels of public reporting forms, checked
  by hand on official sites on 2026-11-09, in data/report_channels.csv. Janus
  links to the forms and never submits anything; use does not imply endorsement
  by any authority.
  No MedDRA term is stored or shown by the report assistant.
  Snapshot: retrieved 2026-11-09 (data/report_channels.csv)

